Scríobh bundles third-party fonts. Each is embedded unmodified, with its licence.

Served to the browser (web/static/fonts, each with its OFL text beside it):
  Newsreader          SIL Open Font License 1.1   OFL-newsreader.txt
  Instrument Sans     SIL Open Font License 1.1   OFL-instrumentsans.txt
  IBM Plex Mono       SIL Open Font License 1.1   OFL-ibmplexmono.txt

Embedded in the binary and set into PDF files (internal/publish/font/data):
  Liberation Serif and Liberation Mono 2.1.5
    Digitized data copyright (c) 2010 Google Corporation.
    Copyright (c) 2012 Red Hat, Inc.
    SIL Open Font License 1.1: OFL-liberation.txt
  DejaVu Serif and DejaVu Sans 2.37 (fallback faces)
    Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc. All Rights Reserved.
    DejaVu changes are in public domain.
    Glyphs imported from Arev fonts are (c) Tavmjong Bah.
    Bitstream Vera licence: LICENSE-dejavu.txt
  Source, versions and SHA-256 hashes: internal/publish/font/data/SOURCES.txt

A PDF written by the program holds a subset of these fonts (the glyphs the
document uses), which the licences allow.
